          "answer": "Based on reading `src/api/routes.py`, here are the three routes:\n\n**1. `GET /stock/<sku>`** (`get_stock`)\n- Decorated with `@require_token` for authentication\n- Takes a request object with an `sku` attribute\n- Returns `{\"sku\": request.sku, \"level\": level_for(request.sku)}`\n- Looks up the current stock level for a single item using `level_for()` from `src/inventory/stock.py`\n\n**2. `POST /stock/<sku>/adjust`** (`post_adjust`)\n- Decorated with `@require_token` for authentication\n- Takes a request object with `sku` and `delta` attributes\n- Returns `{\"sku\": request.sku, \"level\": adjust(request.sku, request.delta)}`\n- Adjusts the stock level up or down by `delta` using `adjust()` from `src/inventory/stock.py`, which also drops the stale cache entry\n\n**3. `GET /reorder`** (`get_reorder`)\n- Decorated with `@require_token` for authentication\n- No request parameters needed beyond authentication\n- Returns `{\"due\": reorder_due()}`\n- Calls `reorder_due()` from `src/inventory/reorder.py`, which returns all SKUs where the current level is at or below the `REORDER_THRESHOLD` (12, from config)",
